  "prompt": "LOCAL UPPER TORSO EDIT of image 1, an existing east-facing running sprite. Return one independent native at least 1024x1024 square RGBA transparent image, same full canvas framing and safe transparent margins. Image 1 is the MAIN image: preserve its head, hair silhouette and size, face, head position, both legs, both knees/boots and every foot contact location, robe hem, pose phase, exact hands and prop locations, TWO cyan ink spirits, and rendering finish. Image 2 is ONLY the required consistent chest-front three-quarter SIDE camera and clothing-front reference; do NOT copy its limb pose. Image 3 is project material/rendering style only, do not reproduce its UI. Repair image1's apparent rear/back shoulder view into the same chest-front oblique EAST-facing torso family as image2 without changing the head or legs. Anatomical RIGHT brush arm is the NEAR arm: its shoulder originates just below the neck toward screen LEFT, the near right sleeve crosses and occludes the chest while reaching toward the existing screen-RIGHT brush hand. Keep that shoulder/elbow/wrist connected; DO NOT swap shoulder ownership or move the brush to the far arm. Anatomical LEFT blank-scroll arm is FAR and swings backward toward existing screen LEFT scroll hand: most upper arm is behind the torso, with only the rear-edge sleeve/hand visible; do NOT expose a broad far shoulder across the back. Change ONLY the upper robe chest/shoulder occlusion and visible waist front: show a narrow white diagonal front lapel edge and appropriately front-facing waist taiji attachment partly obscured by the near crossing sleeve. It is GOOD for the right near sleeve to obscure most chest decoration. Do not force a full frontal chest ornament by exchanging the arms. Do not add an extra arm, hand, prop or spirit. Keep forward lean, scale, camera azimuth, body placement, original legs/boots exactly. All visible hand identity remains RIGHT BRUSH / LEFT BLANK SCROLL. This is one local torso continuity fix, not a new pose or a turnaround. No background, no floor, no text, no crop, no mirroring."
}

